cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this code, cite SkinTokens / TokenRig and the org's ggml port it is vendored from.
title: skin-tokens.cpp, the org's C++23/ggml port of SkinTokens / TokenRig (vendored)
abstract: >-
  git subtree (squashed) of V-Sekai-fire/skin-tokens-ggml at 097a0cc: the
  C++23/ggml port of SkinTokens / TokenRig (automatic skeleton and skin
  weight generation from a static mesh) that the dress-on loop's rig stage
  replaces its FoxGirl rig fixture with (Cut 7). Local adaptations:
  (1) ggml/ (the pinned upstream v0.20.2 copy, 2,133 files, 25 MB) and
  patches/ggml/ (two Vulkan coopmat patches) are deleted: the infer ELF
  carries one ggml, the org's (V-Sekai-fire/ggml; C:/contract-manifest
  2-contract/ggml @04b55bba on the host until Cut 3 lands vendor/ggml), and
  the Vulkan patches do not apply to ggml-cpu or to the RenderingDevice
  backend. cmake/PrepareGGML.cmake and the upstream CMakeLists.txt are kept
  untouched but unused; tests/native/infer/CMakeLists.txt lists the sources
  against the shared ggml instead.
  (2) nlohmann/json (src/glb.cpp only, host GLB I/O) resolves on the host
  from the org's stable-diffusion-ggml thirdparty/json.hpp (3.11.2).
  Later adaptations for the guest ELF (single thread, weights streamed via
  host UPLOAD instead of file paths, ggml backend swapped to ggml-rd) are
  recorded here as they land.
